---
title: "Life OS: one task's Google Calendar event"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    lg0: settled
    lg1: waiting
    lg2: stuck
  }
  class lg0 teal
  class lg1 blue
  class lg2 orange
  s0: Not on the calendar
  s1: Waiting to be added
  s2: On the calendar
  s3: Waiting to be removed
  s4: Marked deleted in Google
  s5: Shows why Google refused
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: you turn sync on or you give it a date or you turn auto-add on
  s1 --> s0: you turn sync off or you take the date away or you turn auto-add off
  s1 --> s2: the push runs or you press Repair
  s2 --> s3: you turn sync off or you take the date away or you turn auto-add off
  s2 --> s4: it is gone in Google
  s3 --> s0: the cleanup runs or the push runs or you press Repair
  s3 --> s5: Google refuses
  s3 --> s2: you turn sync on or you give it a date or you turn auto-add on
  s4 --> s2: you press Repair
  s4 --> s0: you turn auto-add off or the push runs
  s5 --> s3: you take the date away or you turn sync off or you turn auto-add off
  s3 --> s1: the cleanup runs
  s4 --> s1: you give it a date
  s5 --> s0: you press Repair
  s5 --> s2: you give it a date or you press Repair
  class s0 teal
  class s1 blue
  class s2 teal
  class s3 blue
  class s4 orange
  class s5 teal
